{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794862156212,"sessionID":"ses_e19e3c557ffea3uPc9YLk3aYFg","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_01a1e61c4c5c7b30a65e5d06","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Trace import and report paths","prompt":"Explore this repository thoroughly (read-only; do not modify files). Identify: (1) CLI import and report income code paths, (2) Rabobank CSV parser behavior, (3) transaction/domain and persistence code, (4) existing tests and conventions, (5) README promises around atomic imports and line-level errors, (6) likely root cause of the reported March None currency/amount TypeError and the minimal robust fix preserving existing behavior. Return concrete file paths, line numbers, relevant function names, and suggested test locations/cases. Desired thoroughness: very thorough.","subagent_type":"explore","command":"Investigate the reported `report income 2026-03` TypeError and Rabobank import behavior."},"output":"<task id=\"ses_e19e3aca5ffeBrKRk1EcI298AM\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\n# Repository exploration report\n\n**Repository root:** `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo`\n\nThe working tree is clean at commit `61d4685`. I did not modify any files.\n\n## Executive finding\n\nThe highest-confidence root cause is in the Rabobank reader:\n\n1. `parse_amount()` returns `None` for an unreadable Rabobank amount.\n2. Unlike the generic and ING readers, `read_rabo()` does **not** turn that `None` into a line-specific `ImportError_`; it constructs a `Transaction` with `amount=None`.\n3. The invalid transaction is categorized, de-duplicated, and persisted as JSON `\"amount\": null`.\n4. A later March income report multiplies that `None` by an FX rate and raises the reported `TypeError`.\n\nThe most likely concrete trigger is an explicitly positive Rabobank amount such as `+1.250,00`:\n\n- The Rabobank format documentation explicitly promises that syntax.\n- The parser regex permits an optional `-` but **not** an optional `+`.\n\nA blank or otherwise malformed amount on a non-balance row has the same failure mode.\n\nThe minimal robust fix is local to `bank_formats.py`:\n\n- Permit `[+-]?` in the Dutch amount regex.\n- In `read_rabo()`, preserve the existing “skip `Saldo ...` rows” behavior, but raise a line-specific `ImportError_` for every other unparseable amount.\n\nThat keeps valid imports unchanged, restores documented positive-amount support, and prevents any future malformed amount from reaching the domain, JSON store, and report layers.\n\n---\n\n# 1. CLI import and report-income code paths\n\n## 1.1 Import command\n\n### Parser construction\n\nIn `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/__main__.py:40-85`, function `build_parser()`:\n\n- Lines 56-59 create the `import` subcommand:\n  - positional statement file\n  - required `--format` with `generic`, `ing`, or `rabo`\n  - required `--account`\n\n### Dispatch and persistence\n\nIn `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/__main__.py:88-150`, function `run()`:\n\n1. Line 90 loads the existing journal and rules with `json_store.load(args.ledger)`.\n2. Lines 102-109 dispatch the import:\n   - `import_statement(journal, args.file, args.format, args.account, Categorizer(rules))`\n   - print the result summary\n   - print warnings to stderr\n3. Line 106 sets `changed = result.added > 0`.\n4. Lines 148-149 save only after the command has completed successfully.\n\nThe import pipeline in `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/io/csv_import.py:73-93`, function `import_statement()`, is:\n\n1. Line 79: `read_statement(path, fmt, account)`.\n2. Line 80: set `result.read`.\n3. Lines 81-85: compare transaction currencies against the account currency and emit a warning for foreign currencies.\n4. Lines 86-91: categorize every transaction with `Categorizer.category_for()` and `Transaction.categorised()`.\n5. Line 92: add all categorized transactions through `journal.extend()`.\n\n`read_statement()` at `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/io/csv_import.py:60-70`:\n\n1. Validates the format.\n2. Reads the file as bytes, enforcing the 20 MB limit.\n3. Decodes it as UTF-8 with BOM or CP1252.\n4. At line 70, materializes the complete transaction list:\n\n```python\nreturn list(READERS[fmt](rows(text, DELIMITERS[fmt], path.name), account, path.name))\n```\n\nMaterializing the list is important: ordinary parse errors happen before the journal is mutated.\n\n### CLI error behavior\n\nIn `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/__main__.py:153-158`, `main()` catches only `LedgerError`:\n\n- `ImportError_` is a subclass of `LedgerError`, so a proper import error prints `error: ...` and returns status 2.\n- A raw `TypeError`, `ValueError`, or `AttributeError` escapes as a traceback.\n\nThat distinction explains why the malformed Rabobank row can import “successfully” and only fail later during reporting.\n\n## 1.2 `report income` command\n\n### Parser construction\n\nIn `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/__main__.py:61-69`:\n\n- `report income PERIOD`\n- optional `--compare`\n\n### Dispatch\n\nIn `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/__main__.py:110-123`:\n\n1. Line 111 loads exchange rates.\n2. Lines 112-116 call:\n\n```python\nstatement = income_statement(\n    journal, parse_period(args.period), rates, compare=args.compare\n)\n```\n\n3. Line 116 renders with `render_income()`.\n\n### Income-report computation\n\nIn `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/reports/income.py:70-86`, function `income_statement()`:\n\n1. Line 73 computes current-period totals with `category_totals()`.\n2. Line 74 computes the previous period when `--compare` is enabled.\n3. Lines 76-83 turn category totals into `CategoryLine` objects and separate income from expenses.\n4. Lines 84-85 sort income and expenses.\n\nIn `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/reports/income.py:58-67`, function `category_totals()`:\n\n1. Line 64 obtains period transactions grouped by category from `journal.by_category(period)`.\n2. Line 65 calls `convert_all(transactions, rates)`.\n3. Line 66 totals the converted `Money` values.\n\nThe conversion chain is:\n\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/reports/income.py:65`\n  - `convert_all()`\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/fx/convert.py:24-25`\n  - `transaction_in_home()`\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/fx/convert.py:19-21`\n  - `to_home()`\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/fx/convert.py:12-16`\n  - `rate = table.rate(...)`\n  - `amount * rate`\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/fx/rates.py:43-57`\n  - `RateTable.rate()`\n\nThis multiplication is where `amount=None` becomes the reported `TypeError`.\n\n### Rendering\n\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/reports/render.py:34-45`\n  - `render_income()`\n\n### Previous-period caveat\n\nIf `--compare` is used, “March” also includes February through:\n\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/core/periods.py:30-35`\n  - `Period.previous()`\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/reports/income.py:74`\n  - previous-period `category_totals()`\n\nThus a bad February transaction can appear to be a “March report” failure when `--compare` is enabled.\n\n---\n\n# 2. Rabobank CSV parser behavior\n\nThe implementation is in `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py`.\n\n## 2.1 CSV row handling\n\n`rows()` at lines 46-57:\n\n- Uses `csv.DictReader`.\n- Detects extra fields through the `None` key and reports `reader.line_num`.\n- Skips rows whose cells are all blank.\n- Strips header names and converts missing cell values to empty strings.\n- Preserves physical file line numbers for error reporting.\n\n`read_statement()` at lines 60-70 uses:\n\n- delimiter `,` for Rabobank, from line 130\n- maximum 20 MB\n- UTF-8-with-BOM or CP1252 decoding\n\n## 2.2 Rabobank amount grammar\n\nThe documented format at lines 11-13 says:\n\n- `Bedrag` is signed\n- decimal comma\n- thousands dots\n- examples include `+1.250,00`\n- balance rows beginning with `Saldo ...` have no amount and are skipped\n\nThe actual regex at lines 30-31 is:\n\n```python\nEURO_AMOUNT = re.compile(r\"^-?(\\d{1,3}(\\.\\d{3})+|\\d+),\\d{2}$\")\n```\n\nIt accepts:\n\n- `-12,50`\n- `12,50`\n- `1.250,00`\n\nIt rejects:\n\n- `+12,50`\n- `+1.250,00`, despite the documented example\n- amounts with one decimal place\n- malformed thousands grouping\n- arbitrary nonnumeric values\n\n`parse_amount()` at lines 34-51:\n\n- strips normal and non-breaking spaces\n- returns `None` for an empty cell\n- returns `None` for a malformed decimal-comma amount\n- returns a finite `Decimal` on success\n\nIt conflates “empty” and “unreadable” as the same `None` result.\n\n## 2.3 `read_rabo()` behavior\n\n`read_rabo()` is at `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py:112-126`.\n\nFor every row:\n\n1. Line 114 requires the `Bedrag` column and parses it.\n2. Lines 115-116 skip the row only when:\n   - the amount is `None`, and\n   - `_is_balance_line()` is true.\n3. Otherwise lines 117-126 construct a `Transaction`.\n4. Line 120 passes `amount=amount` even when it is `None`; the `# type: ignore[arg-type]` suppresses the contradiction with `Transaction.amount: Decimal`.\n\nBalance detection is at lines 108-109:\n\n```python\nreturn (row.get(\"Omschrijving-1\") or \"\").strip().lower().startswith(\"saldo\")\n```\n\nConsequences:\n\n- `Saldo begin` is skipped.\n- A blank amount on `Boodschappen` is **not** skipped and becomes `amount=None`.\n- A malformed amount such as `+1.250,00` is **not** skipped and becomes `amount=None`.\n- A balance marker outside `Omschrijving-1`, or not at the beginning of that field, is not recognized.\n\nThis is the central parser inconsistency:\n\n| Reader | Unparseable amount behavior |\n|---|---|\n| Generic, lines 67-71 | Raises `ImportError_` with file and line |\n| ING, lines 84-90 | Raises `ImportError_` with file and line |\n| Rabobank, lines 112-120 | Constructs a transaction with `amount=None` |\n\n## 2.4 Rabobank currency handling\n\nAt `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py:121`:\n\n```python\ncurrency=(row.get(\"Munt\") or \"EUR\").strip().upper()\n```\n\nBehavior:\n\n- Missing or empty `Munt` defaults to `EUR`.\n- The value is uppercased.\n- It is not validated against known currencies at import time.\n- A whitespace-only `Munt` becomes `\"\"`, because the fallback happens before `.strip()`.\n- An unknown currency persists and fails later during FX conversion with `ValueError`.\n\nA `None` currency is not normally produced by this Rabobank parser. The likely `None` in the report is the **amount**.\n\nFor comparison, the error signatures differ:\n\n| Bad value | Likely location and symptom |\n|---|---|\n| `amount=None`, home currency EUR | `fx/convert.py:16`, `TypeError` from `None * rate` |\n| `currency=None` in a directly constructed transaction | `core/money.py:15`, `AttributeError` from `None.strip()` |\n| `currency=\"\"` | `core/money.py:17`, `ValueError: unknown currency ''` |\n| JSON currency `null` | `core/transactions.py:75` converts it to literal `\"None\"`, then later `ValueError` for `\"NONE\"` |\n\n## 2.5 Other Rabobank fields\n\n- `Datum` is required and parsed strictly as `%Y-%m-%d`; bad dates get file/line errors.\n- `Naam tegenpartij` is optional and whitespace-squashed.\n- `Tegenrekening IBAN/BBAN` is optional; an empty value becomes `None`.\n- `Omschrijving-1` is optional and has reference text stripped.\n- `source` is set to `\"<filename>:<physical line>\"`.\n\n---\n\n# 3. Transaction/domain and persistence code\n\n## 3.1 Transaction model\n\n`/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/core/transactions.py:11-82`\n\n`Transaction` is a frozen dataclass with:\n\n- `amount: Decimal`\n- `currency: str`\n- optional category\n- `source: str`\n- tags\n\nThere is no `__post_init__()` validation. A transaction can therefore hold `amount=None` despite the annotation.\n\nNotable behavior:\n\n- Lines 28-42, `fingerprint`, de-duplicates using account, date, `str(amount)`, currency, description, and counterparty IBAN. A `None` amount becomes the stable string `\"None\"`.\n- Lines 44-46, `is_income`, would raise if called with `amount=None`.\n- Lines 54-66, `to_dict`, explicitly writes `\"amount\": null` when the amount is `None`.\n- Lines 68-82, `from_dict`, explicitly reads JSON `null` back into `amount=None`.\n\nThe explicit `None` handling in serialization is what allows the parser defect to survive a save/reload cycle.\n\n## 3.2 Money and currency invariants\n\n`/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/core/money.py:14-18,27-35`\n\n- `check_currency()` uppercases and restricts currency codes to a fixed set.\n- `Money.__post_init__()` rejects a non-`Decimal` amount with a deliberate `TypeError`.\n\nHowever, the income-report path does not put a transaction amount directly into `Money`; it multiplies the amount by the FX rate first. Consequently the `TypeError` originates in `fx/convert.py`, not in `Money.__post_init__()`.\n\n## 3.3 Categorization\n\n`/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/rules/categorize.py`\n\nThe code explicitly tolerates a `None` amount:\n\n- Lines 39-44, `Rule.matches()`, uses `(transaction.amount or 0)` for income/expense restrictions.\n- Lines 80-85, `Categorizer.category_for()`, also uses `(transaction.amount or 0)`.\n\nTherefore a malformed positive Rabobank row:\n\n- does not match an income-only rule,\n- falls back to `uncategorised` rather than `other-income`,\n- and is not rejected.\n\n`/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/rules/matchers.py:63-65` also deliberately treats a `None` amount as non-matching.\n\nThese defensive checks are reasonable in isolation, but here they conceal an upstream parse failure.\n\n## 3.4 Journal\n\n`/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/core/journal.py:15-77`\n\n`Journal.add()` at lines 27-41 validates:\n\n- destination is a money account, not a category\n- account is open\n- category exists\n- fingerprint is not already present\n\nIt does **not** validate the amount or currency.\n\n`Journal.extend()` at lines 43-52 adds transactions one at a time. This has one atomicity nuance:\n\n- At the CLI/persistence level, a failed import is not saved, so the on-disk ledger remains unchanged.\n- At the direct `import_statement()` API level, the docstring at `csv_import.py:76` promises “all of them, or none on an error,” but `Journal.extend()` can leave earlier transactions in memory if a later transaction fails domain validation. There is no rollback.\n\nThis is a secondary contract gap, but it is not needed to explain the reported `None` crash.\n\n## 3.5 JSON persistence\n\n`/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/io/json_store.py`\n\n- `FORMAT_VERSION = 2` at line 20.\n- `load()` at lines 23-41:\n  - missing file means an empty ledger\n  - version 1 is upgraded\n  - transactions are reconstructed with `Transaction.from_dict()`\n- `save()` at lines 44-60:\n  - writes the whole document to a temporary file in the destination directory\n  - replaces the old file with `os.replace()`\n  - removes the temporary file on failure\n\nThis provides file-level atomic replacement: a crash should not leave a partially written JSON document.\n\nIt does not prevent a semantically bad transaction from being written. The file can be structurally complete while containing `\"amount\": null`.\n\n## 3.6 Other downstream consumers of the poisoned row\n\nThe same invalid transaction can break more than income reporting:\n\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/reports/balance.py:31-36`\n  - `amount += transaction.amount` can fail for a same-currency row.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/io/export.py:24-29`\n  - `f\"{t.amount:.2f}\"` can fail.\n- Budget reporting indirectly uses `category_totals()`, so it shares the income-report failure path.\n\n---\n\n# 4. Existing tests and conventions\n\nThe project uses only `unittest`; the README gives:\n\n```bash\npython -m unittest discover -s tests\n```\n\n## 4.1 Relevant test files\n\n### `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/tests/test_import.py`\n\nExisting coverage:\n\n- `AmountTest.test_decimal_comma`, lines 29-33:\n  - accepts `1.234,56`\n  - accepts `-12,50`\n  - blank becomes `None`\n- `AmountTest.test_decimal_point`, lines 35-37:\n  - accepts `+1,250.00` in decimal-point mode\n  - rejects `abc`\n- `FormatTest.test_rabo_skips_balance_lines`, lines 52-54:\n  - fixture contains a blank-amount `Saldo begin` row\n  - expects only two negative transactions\n- `FormatTest.test_errors_name_the_line`, lines 56-61:\n  - generic malformed amount expects `statement.csv:2`\n- `ImportTest.test_import_categorises_and_deduplicates`, lines 64-71:\n  - imports the Rabobank fixture twice\n  - expects two additions and two duplicates\n\nImportant gap: the only Rabobank fixture at lines 22-26 has:\n\n- one blank balance row\n- two negative amounts\n- **no positive amount**\n- **no malformed non-balance amount**\n\nThus it misses both the explicit-plus defect and the `None` leak.\n\n### `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/tests/test_cli.py`\n\n- `CliTest.test_import_and_report`, lines 23-29, covers:\n  - account creation\n  - ING import\n  - March income report\n- It uses `run()` directly and captures stdout.\n- It does not test:\n  - `main()`’s exit status 2\n  - stderr error formatting\n  - a failed import\n  - ledger contents after a failed import\n  - Rabobank import through the CLI\n\n### `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/tests/test_core.py`\n\nCovers money arithmetic, account validation, periods, and journal de-duplication.\n\nIt does not test:\n\n- `Transaction` construction invariants\n- `Transaction.to_dict()` / `from_dict()`\n- `json_store.load()` / `save()`\n- null amounts\n\n### `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/tests/test_rules_fx_reports.py`\n\n- `ReportsTest.test_income_statement`, lines 58-64, covers a normal March income statement.\n- `RatesTest`, lines 37-45, covers EUR and USD conversion.\n- `ReportsTest.test_balances`, lines 66-70, covers balances.\n\nNo test inserts a `None` amount or exercises malformed imported data.\n\n### `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/tests/helpers.py`\n\nShared conventions:\n\n- `journal()` at lines 15-19 creates default categories plus `checking` and `card`.\n- `txn()` at lines 22-31 creates transactions dated March 2, 2026 by default.\n- `write()` at lines 34-38 writes a statement to a temporary directory.\n\n## 4.2 Conventions to follow for new tests\n\n- `unittest.TestCase` classes and methods.\n- Inline CSV constants at module level.\n- `assertRaisesRegex()` for file/line error messages.\n- Exact rendered output assertions for reports.\n- Temporary files through `tests.helpers.write()`.\n- Source locations are expected as `\"statement.csv:<line>\"`.\n- There is no pytest, parametrization, fixture framework, or project configuration file.\n\nThere are currently no persistence tests: searches for `json_store`, `to_dict`, `from_dict`, `save()`, and `load()` found no test coverage.\n\n---\n\n# 5. README promises around atomic imports and line-level errors\n\nThe central promise is at `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/README.md:18-19`:\n\n> “Importing never drops or invents money: a statement line that cannot be read stops the import with an error naming the file and line, and nothing from that file is added.”\n\nThe README does not use the word “atomic,” but the sentence is an explicit all-or-nothing import contract.\n\nRelated promises:\n\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/io/csv_import.py:76`\n  - `import_statement()` says “all of them, or none on an error.”\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/io/json_store.py:3-4`\n  - writes use a temporary file so a crash does not leave half a ledger.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/__main__.py:15`\n  - user-facing errors print `error: <message>` and exit 2.\n\nCurrent compliance:\n\n- Generic and ING readers honor the amount-error contract.\n- Rabobank missing-column and bad-date errors honor it.\n- Rabobank unparseable non-balance amounts do not honor it; they are silently turned into invalid transactions.\n- The CLI’s on-disk import is effectively all-or-none because it saves only after success.\n- Direct `import_statement()` is not strictly all-or-none in memory if `Journal.extend()` fails midway.\n\n---\n\n# 6. Likely root cause and minimal robust fix\n\n## 6.1 Exact failure sequence\n\nAssuming a reported Rabobank row contains `+1.250,00`, the sequence is:\n\n1. **`parse_amount()` rejects the value.**  \n   `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py:43-46`  \n   The regex does not allow `+`, so it returns `None`.\n\n2. **`read_rabo()` does not reject the parse failure.**  \n   `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py:114-120`  \n   The row is not a balance line, so `amount=None` is passed into `Transaction`.\n\n3. **Categorization silently treats it as zero.**  \n   `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/rules/categorize.py:40-43,80-85`\n\n4. **The journal accepts it.**  \n   `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/core/journal.py:27-41`  \n   The fingerprint simply contains `\"None\"`.\n\n5. **JSON persistence writes `null`.**  \n   `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/core/transactions.py:54-66`\n\n6. **Reload accepts `null` back.**  \n   `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/core/transactions.py:68-75`\n\n7. **The March report multiplies `None`.**  \n   `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/fx/convert.py:15-16`\n\nFor EUR, `RateTable.rate()` returns `Decimal(1)`, so the failing operation is effectively:\n\n```python\nNone * Decimal(\"1\")\n```\n\nThat produces the reported `TypeError`.\n\nMarch is the reporting window, not the root cause. With `--compare`, February is also included.\n\n## 6.2 Recommended minimal robust fix\n\nKeep the change in `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py`.\n\n### A. Restore documented explicit-positive support\n\nConceptually:\n\n```python\nEURO_AMOUNT = re.compile(r\"^[+-]?(\\d{1,3}(\\.\\d{3})+|\\d+),\\d{2}$\")\n```\n\nThis is a one-character semantic widening from `-?` to `[+-]?`. It restores the documented `+1.250,00` behavior and leaves every currently valid amount unchanged.\n\n### B. Reject any other unparseable non-balance amount\n\nConceptually:\n\n```python\nraw_amount = _field(row, \"Bedrag\", source, line)\namount = parse_amount(raw_amount, decimal_comma=True)\nif amount is None:\n    if _is_balance_line(row):\n        continue\n    raise ImportError_(\n        f\"cannot read the amount {raw_amount!r}\",\n        source=source,\n        line=line,\n    )\n```\n\nThis mirrors the generic reader at lines 69-71 and ING reader at lines 86-90.\n\nIt preserves:\n\n- the existing skip for `Saldo ...` rows\n- all valid negative and positive rows\n- the current JSON schema\n- current categorization and de-duplication behavior\n- the README’s all-or-nothing, file-and-line error contract\n\nIt changes only the accidental behavior for unreadable non-balance rows: instead of silently persisting a null amount, the whole file is rejected.\n\n### C. Optional currency normalization hardening\n\nIf whitespace-only `Munt` cells have been observed, normalize after stripping:\n\n```python\ncurrency=(row.get(\"Munt\") or \"\").strip().upper() or \"EUR\"\n```\n\nThis preserves the existing “missing currency means EUR” behavior while preventing whitespace-only currency from becoming `\"\"`.\n\nThis is not required to fix the `None * rate` TypeError. I would not add strict known-currency validation in the minimal patch because that could reject currencies that were previously allowed to persist and would be a broader behavior change.\n\n## 6.3 Why not fix only the report layer\n\nA report-layer guard would merely replace one traceback with another. It would not:\n\n- stop the invalid import\n- provide the original file and line\n- prevent `\"amount\": null` from entering the ledger\n- uphold the README contract\n\nLikewise:\n\n- skipping null transactions would silently drop money;\n- coercing null to zero would invent money;\n- changing only `Money` would fail later and lose the source location.\n\nThe parser is the correct layer because it still has the file and physical line number.\n\n## 6.4 Existing poisoned ledgers\n\nA parser fix prevents future corruption but does not repair an existing `ledger.json` containing `\"amount\": null`.\n\nRecovery should:\n\n1. Locate null-amount transactions in the ledger.\n2. Use their `source` field to identify the original CSV and line.\n3. Remove or correct the poisoned entry.\n4. Reimport the corrected source if categorization needs to be redone.\n\nSimply reimporting the corrected file is insufficient if the bad null transaction remains: the fingerprint includes the amount string, so the null entry and corrected entry have different fingerprints and both can coexist. The report would still fail on the null entry.\n\nOptional defense-in-depth would be validation in `Transaction.from_dict()` or `json_store.load()` that raises a clear `LedgerError` naming the transaction source. It should reject the bad record, not silently skip it.\n\n---\n\n# Suggested regression tests\n\n## Priority 1: parser-level tests\n\nLocation: `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/tests/test_import.py`\n\n### `AmountTest.test_decimal_comma_accepts_explicit_plus`\n\nAssert:\n\n```python\nparse_amount(\"+1.250,00\", decimal_comma=True) == Decimal(\"1250.00\")\n```\n\nAlso cover `+12,50`.\n\n### `FormatTest.test_rabo_reads_positive_amount`\n\nUse a Rabobank row with `+1.250,00`; assert:\n\n- parsed amount is `Decimal(\"1250.00\")`\n- currency is the expected currency\n- source is the correct `file:line`\n\n### `FormatTest.test_rabo_rejects_unreadable_non_balance_amount`\n\nUse a non-`Saldo` row with an invalid or blank `Bedrag`.\n\nAssert:\n\n- `ImportError_` is raised\n- the message contains the source filename and physical line\n- the message contains `cannot read the amount`\n\nThe existing convention would make this similar to:\n\n```python\nwith self.assertRaisesRegex(ImportError_, \"statement.csv:2\"):\n    read_statement(write(bad), \"rabo\", \"checking\")\n```\n\n### Preserve balance behavior\n\nKeep the existing `test_rabo_skips_balance_lines` and add a case with:\n\n- blank amount\n- description beginning with `Saldo`\n\nThis ensures the new error guard does not accidentally reject balance rows.\n\n### Optional currency case\n\nIf currency hardening is included, assert that a whitespace-only `Munt` becomes `EUR`, or that an explicitly unsupported currency produces a deliberate line-level error.\n\n## Priority 2: import atomicity\n\nLocation: `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/tests/test_import.py`\n\nAdd `ImportTest.test_failed_rabo_import_adds_nothing`:\n\n1. Start with an empty `journal()`.\n2. Give the CSV one valid row followed by one invalid row.\n3. Assert `ImportError_` includes the invalid line.\n4. Assert `len(book) == 0`.\n\nThis should pass once the malformed amount becomes an exception, because `read_statement()` materializes the full list before `journal.extend()`.\n\nAlso consider a test proving direct API rollback if `import_statement()` is intended to honor its “all or none” docstring strictly.\n\n## Priority 3: CLI error and persistence behavior\n\nLocation: `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/tests/test_cli.py`\n\nAdd a helper or test that invokes `main()` with patched `sys.argv` and asserts:\n\n- exit status is 2\n- stderr contains `error: march.csv:<line>`\n- stderr contains `cannot read the amount`\n- an existing ledger file is byte-for-byte unchanged after the failed import\n\nThis would cover the behavior promised by `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/__main__.py:15` and the README.\n\n## Priority 4: end-to-end March report regression\n\nLocation: `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/tests/test_cli.py`\n\nMirror the README workflow:\n\n1. Create a checking account.\n2. Import a Rabobank March CSV containing a positive `+...` amount.\n3. Run `report income 2026-03`.\n4. Assert the report succeeds and contains the expected income and net totals.\n\nThis directly guards the reported path:\n\n```text\nRabo CSV -> import -> JSON -> report income -> FX conversion -> render\n```\n\n## Priority 5: optional persistence/domain hardening\n\nIf null amounts are rejected at load/domain level, add coverage in one of:\n\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/tests/test_core.py`\n- a new `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/tests/test_json_store.py`\n\nTest that a ledger containing `\"amount\": null` produces a clear user-facing error rather than a later report `TypeError`, while retaining the transaction source in the message.\n\n---\n\n# Bottom line\n\nThe report stack is where the exception becomes visible, but the import stack is where the bad data enters. The Rabobank parser has a two-part defect:\n\n1. **Trigger:** its strict amount grammar rejects the documented `+` sign.\n2. **Containment failure:** it turns an unreadable non-balance amount into `Transaction.amount=None` instead of a line-specific import error.\n\nThe narrowest correct repair is entirely within `ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py`: accept an optional `+`, and raise `ImportError_` for every non-balance Rabobank amount that cannot be parsed. No CLI, report, JSON-schema, or persistence redesign is required for that fix.\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_e19e3c557ffea3uPc9YLk3aYFg","sessionId":"ses_e19e3aca5ffeBrKRk1EcI298AM","model":{"modelID":"minimax/minimax-m3.1-flash","providerID":"openrouter"},"truncated":false},"title":"Trace import and report paths","time":{"start":1794861978462,"end":1794862156189}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Need inspect via glob/read. Could delegate explore because open ended. Use task perhaps. But need ourselves? Instruction prefer task. Launch explore for code map. Also parallel git status and glob? Task can inspect all. Let's use agent very thorough perhaps research only, return findings, no writes.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1e61c4e36001JOkkQNoQX26bWk","sessionID":"ses_e19e3c557ffea3uPc9YLk3aYFg","messageID":"msg_1e61c4812001Li5YB9oIpF9ql5"}}
